      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Corner-detection comparison playground\n\nTwo classic corner detectors run off the SAME photo (fed straight in - the gray-only wrappers auto-grayscale a ComfyUI IMAGE):\n\nLEFT - cv2.cornerHarris returns a dense RESPONSE MAP (a float score per pixel, high at corners); 'Preview CV Array' in heatmap mode shows where the corner energy concentrates. It is a map, not a list - you would threshold + non-max-suppress it to get discrete points.\n\nRIGHT - cv2.goodFeaturesToTrack (Shi-Tomasi) instead returns a ready LIST of the strongest corners (blue rings). cv2.cornerSubPix then refines each one to SUB-PIXEL accuracy by fitting the local gradient - the refined points (small vermillion dots) sit a fraction of a pixel off the integer detections, which are drawn as larger blue RINGS. Zoom the overlay to see the split - the ring/dot difference is what carries it, so it survives colour blindness and a greyscale print.\n\nA low-texture photo simply yields fewer corners; nothing fails. (Note: cv2.cornerSubPix itself requires at least one corner - gate it behind 'if/else' on the corner count for a pipeline that must accept blanks.)"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
